  "story": {
    "id": "marta_photo_walk",
    "person_id": "marta_silva",
    "title": "Photo walk, second traffic",
    "summary": "Marta explores the plaza with a camera and discovers sidewalk robots mid-frame — curiosity dips into cautious neutrality.",
    "beats": [
      {
        "id": "setup",
        "text": "Marta leaves the hotel with a half-charged phone and a list of \"local texture\" shots for a conference talk. She expects cars, bikes, crowds — not machines sharing the footpath.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "approach",
        "text": "The plaza light is good. She frames a cafe awning, then a fountain. A soft whir enters the shot from the right; she lowers the phone, laughing once — \"oh, cute.\"\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "encounter",
        "text": "The bot does not stay cute. It cuts across her intended path toward a hotel service door, pausing where tour groups cluster. Marta steps back into a stranger, apologizes twice, and loses the shot.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "reaction",
        "text": "She tries to guess the bot's next move from its lights and fails. Without local norms, every pause feels like a trap. She hugs the building line and lets three machines pass before crossing again.\n"
      },
      {
        "id": "outcome",
        "text": "Back at the hotel she adds a slide: \"Sidewalk AV is infrastructure, not novelty — sign it like traffic.\" Her comfort settles at cautious neutral: she will share the city, but she wants a map of the rules.\n"
      }
    ],
